member.summary:
A one time token sent to a user's e-mail address (verification, password reset). Only the SHA-256 hash is stored;
the token itself exists only in the e-mail. A token is used once () and expires after
. Issuing a new token of the same purpose retires the older ones.

A product sold inside an app, store neutral, as last synced from the store: App Store subscriptions and In-App
Purchases, Play subscriptions (with base plans in ) and one-time products (purchase options in
). Writes never start from this row: a plan reads the store live and fingerprints what it changes.
